
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.VecMag(Vector: vector): number`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`float llVecMag(vector Vector);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p class="deprecated-text"><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>Deprecated:  use vector.magnitude because It's a fastcall.</span></p>
      <p>  <p>Returns a float that is the magnitude of the vector (the undirected non-negative distance from <b>vec</b> to &lt;0.0, 0.0, 0.0&gt;).</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Vector / vec</td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>math</li>
        <li>math_3d</li>
        <li>vector</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">12</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-pure">Side-Effect Free</span>
        <span class="lua-section attr-label bg-deprecated">Lua Deprecated</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    local input = vector(1.0, 2.0, 3.0)
    ll.Say(0, "The magnitude of " .. tostring(input) .. " is " .. tostring(ll.VecMag(input)) .. ".")
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default {
    state_entry()
    {
        vector input = <1.0,2.0,3.0>;
        llSay(0,"The magnitude of "+(string)input+" is "+(string)llVecMag(input) + ".");
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Mathematically the formula for vector magnitude is
    <ul>
      <li>`[llSqrt](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSqrt)(vec.x * vec.x + vec.y * vec.y + vec.z * vec.z)`</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
    <li>Knowing this, there are ways to circumvent llVecMag for more efficient code.
    <ul>
      <li>vec*vec &lt; 16.0 is over twice as fast as llVecMag(vec) &lt; 4.0.</li>
      <li>vec<i>vec &lt; (dist</i>dist) is about twice as fast as llVecMag(vec) &lt; dist.</li>
      <li>This can work in many other ways, too, with other comparisons.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
